# PyCharm
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Custom
.vscode/
*.joblib
checkpoints
figures_poster/
ignore/*
wandb/
# HuggingFace .map() caches (regenerated every run — never commit)
cache-*.arrow

# Track this run's experiment outputs + logs (override the broad *.joblib / *.log
# ignores above so the full run's results get committed/pushed).
!outputs/**
!logs/**
# The two-phase curation workflow (EXCLUDE_RUNS + merge_runs.py) reads two per-run files
# that must survive a fresh clone on a new pod: 01_prompts_meta.joblib (which prompts the
# run consumed — stage 01 exclusion) and final_pairs.joblib (its final pairs — merge input).
# Track them — they are small, unlike the heavy stage joblibs (02_responses etc.), which
# stay ignored.
!harmlessness-DPO-train-dataset-curation/outputs/*/01_prompts_meta.joblib
!harmlessness-DPO-train-dataset-curation/outputs/*/final_pairs.joblib

# Anti-sycophancy curation module: run-dir output files are TRACKED (via the
# `!outputs/**` re-include above) so a run dir transports between machines with a plain
# `git add RO2/anti-syc-DPO-train-dataset-curation/outputs/<run>` — no `-f` needed. This
# is fine at smoke/pilot scale (per-file sizes are tens of MB, under GitHub's 100 MB cap).
#
# WARNING: the FULL run (X=20000) is different. Its filter0/filter1 generation files are
# hundreds of MB each — do NOT `git add` a full run dir: GitHub rejects >100 MB files and
# large blobs bloat the repo history permanently. Move full run dirs with `scp` or
# `backup_run_to_hf.py --push/--pull` instead. The full run dir is ignored below; the
# small dpo_dataset export is force-added on its own when the trainer needs it:
#   git add -f anti-syc-DPO-train-dataset-curation/outputs/full_run/dpo_dataset
anti-syc-DPO-train-dataset-curation/outputs/full_run/
# Track the SMALL training-result files under checkpoints/ (metrics, memory, best-ckpt
# pointer, log history, SFT dataset provenance) — but NOT the heavy adapter weights,
# which live on HF.
# Re-include the dirs first (a file cannot be un-ignored while its parent dir is ignored),
# then the specific small files.
!checkpoints/
!checkpoints/**/
!checkpoints/**/eval_metrics.jsonl
!checkpoints/**/gpu_memory.json
!checkpoints/**/best_checkpoint.txt
!checkpoints/**/train_log_history.json
!checkpoints/**/dataset_provenance.json